From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:55:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: venc: zero-initialise the v2 QP range

venc_set_properties() sends struct hfi_quantization_range_v2 with only some fields set; the rest is stack garbage.
The SM8150 firmware hung on it. Initialise the struct.

This patch was written by Claude (Anthropic's AI assistant) under the direction of Bryson, who reviewed and
tested it on a Surface Duo.

Signed-off-by: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
index b478b982a..b9701b54f 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
@@ -664,7 +664,7 @@ static int venc_set_properties(struct venus_inst *inst)
 	struct hfi_idr_period idrp;
 	struct hfi_quantization quant;
 	struct hfi_quantization_range quant_range;
-	struct hfi_quantization_range_v2 quant_range_v2;
+	struct hfi_quantization_range_v2 quant_range_v2 = {};
 	struct hfi_enable en;
 	struct hfi_ltr_mode ltr_mode;
 	struct hfi_intra_refresh intra_refresh = {};
